==== a component the base suppresses
# apps/flatpak

Installs flatpak and enables the remotes an image asks for

## Where it is built

Nowhere. suppressed lists it and builds no layer for it: everything it provides, that base already ships.

## What it exchanges

| Direction | What | With |
| --- | --- | --- |
| provides | `flatpak` | apps/browser |

## What it declares to install

| Family | Packages | Enabled repository |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fedora` | `flatpak` | default |

## What it claims

| Benchmark | Rules |
| --- | --- |
| `cis-fedora` | 9.9.9.9 |

A claim the tool records rather than certifies. The scan is what confirms it.

## Where it came from

| Content | Hash |
| --- | --- |
| declared | `9e56d97f0dfcb562688123d30e588de8e86ca7e2c21b1a0a179f11968799046b` |

It was written in this repository, so no library holds a version to compare it against.

## What it pulls in

Nothing. It declares no `asset`.

## Third-party repositories

None. It declares no `copr` and ships no `repo.sh` file.

==== and the same component in an image that does build it
# apps/flatpak

Installs flatpak and enables the remotes an image asks for

## Where it is built

also. suppressed lists it and builds no layer for it: everything it provides, that base already ships.

## Which variant it builds

`also` builds variant `beta`, the default.

## How its options are set

| Build | Option | Set by | Value |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `also` | `remotes` | `beta` | sets "flathub", "flathub-beta" |

==== and one whose manifest never loaded
`apps/flatpak` is listed but was not read
  help: the problem reading it is above
